# The UTF-8 BOM on the Windows sources is load-bearing, not decoration: Windows
# PowerShell reads a BOM-less file in the machine's ANSI code page, and without
# the BOM the em dash in the menu labels decodes into a curly quote that ends
# the string early and breaks the installer. Git stores the BOM as ordinary
# content - these rules only pin line endings, and must never be extended with
# an encoding filter that would strip it.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cs  text eol=crlf

*.sh    text eol=lf
*.swift text eol=lf
*.md    text
